7.9.m:
The mighty Vāyu swiftly rushed against Vipracitti; / Aṃśa was engaged with Saṃvara, and Bhaga with Bala;
Pūṣan [fought] with Virocana, and then Mitra engaged with Bali; / Varuṇa [fought] together with Bāṇa, and Yama together with Andhaka;
Ilvala [fought] together with Jayanta, and the Moon together with Maya; / Rāhu [fought] with Ahirbudhnya, and Kāpālī with Śataketu;
Ajaikapāt [fought] Kālanemi, and Jvara [fought] with Kārtasvana; / Aryaman together with Prahlāda, and Dhara indeed with Anuhlāda;

Unnoticed, all of them fell upon him;
one, crushing his crown, fell to the ground;
another knocked the terrible bow from his hands;
another hurled his firm, divine flagstaff to the ground;
another, striking the chariot, ground it into dust;
and other clubs fell on his chest, thighs, belly, and waist.
Falling, exceedingly terrible and fearsome, they caused him torment.
Thus deprived of his chariot by that wise [demon] with great effort,
Varuṇa left him and went to another battleground.
Yama approached Andhaka, who challenged him, saying, "Halt, halt!"
Then he hurled his rod against his chariot.
